235 0 obj
<<
/Title (This is not a prediction. It is already the established pattern. MIT's NANDA initiative found that 95% of enterprise AI pilots deliver no measurable financial return, based on 150 leadership interviews, surveys of 350 employees and analysis of 300 public deployments. McKinsey's 2025 global survey of nearly 2,000 companies found that only 6% have reached the threshold of significant AI value at enterprise level. The majority have yet to see any measurable bottom-line impact at all. 42% of companies abandoned most of their AI initiatives in 2025, up from 17% the year before.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 130 0 R
/Prev 183 0 R
/Next 290 0 R
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Title (What is missing is not another explanation. It is a category. A distinct layer of organisational performance that determines whether AI investment produces value, and that layer has been almost entirely absent from the tools, frameworks and diagnostics that organisations have been using to assess their readiness.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 130 0 R
/Prev 291 0 R
/Next 184 0 R
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Title (When an AI programme stalls, four explanations are consistently reached for.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 185 0 R
/Next 292 0 R
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Title (We have almost no systematic understanding of whether organisations are capable of realising the value of their AI investment.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 185 0 R
/Prev 293 0 R
>>
endobj
