/Title (These are not the statistics of a technology in its infancy. They are the statistics of a systemic failure to understand where the real problem lies.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 130 0 R
/Prev 235 0 R
/Next 324 0 R
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Title (The answers being offered are familiar. The technology is not mature enough. The data is not clean enough. The talent is not there. Change management was not done well. Governance is lagging deployment. Each of these explanations carries partial truth. Each shares the same fundamental flaw: they locate the problem in the wrong place.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 130 0 R
/Prev 325 0 R
/Next 236 0 R
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Title (The first is the technology argument. The model was not fit for purpose. The integration was too complex. The vendor overpromised. This has the advantage of being fixable. Replace the technology, run the programme again. Yet organisations that have replaced their AI infrastructure entirely frequently report exactly the same stall point. The technology changed. The outcome did not. Something else was the constraint.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 185 0 R
/Prev 237 0 R
/Next 326 0 R
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Title (What the research now confirms is this: leadership failure is the primary cause of AI project failure, ahead of technology, data quality, or skills gaps. RAND Corporation's research, drawing on structured interviews with experienced data scientists and engineers across industries, found that the most common cause is not a technical)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 185 0 R
/Prev 327 0 R
/First 328 0 R
/Last 329 0 R
/Count -3
/Next 238 0 R
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Title (A pattern has emerged across the AI transformation wave that is now consistent enough to name directly. It shows up in financial services firms with mature AI strategies. It shows up in professional services organisations with sophisticated technology functions. It shows up in conglomerates with full board commitment and significant investment. The common thread is not the sector, the scale, or the technology stack. It is the state of the human system.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 239 0 R
/Next 330 0 R
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Title (return if other conditions are not in place. The organisations generating durable AI advantage are not, in the main, the ones with the most advanced models or the largest AI budgets. They are the ones where the human layer was ready. Where the organisation knew what it was deploying toward, where leadership behaviour matched the stated ambition, and where the structures and culture gave people genuine permission to change how they worked.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 239 0 R
/Prev 331 0 R
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Title (The failure pattern presents differently depending on where in the human system the gap sits. But beneath the variation, it is consistently the same problem.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 240 0 R
/Next 332 0 R
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Title (The third form is cultural contradiction. The workforce is willing. Curiosity about AI is present, and the resistance most leaders anticipate is largely absent. The tools are available. Training has been completed. Adoption remains shallow because the reward structures and performance frameworks point in a different direction from the stated  strategy. People understand what they are supposed to do. They can see that doing it)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 240 0 R
/Prev 333 0 R
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Title (will not be rewarded, and might be penalised. The permission has not been genuinely granted, regardless of what the communications said.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 186 0 R
/Prev 240 0 R
/Next 241 0 R
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Title (Three tests sit beneath that question.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 131 0 R
/Prev 242 0 R
/Next 334 0 R
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Title (And does the workforce have not just the capability but the genuine conditions to work alongside AI as a collaborator?)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 131 0 R
/Prev 335 0 R
/Next 243 0 R
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Title (The gap between AI investment and AI value is closable. But not by doing more of what has already failed to close it.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 132 0 R
/Prev 244 0 R
/Next 245 0 R
>>
endobj
